[stderr] # 02 — Feature model, domains, journeys, and release slices
[stderr] 
[stderr] **Inputs:** `INITIAL.md`, `PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, F001 discovery, and game identity.
[stderr] This model resolves the generic story/battle wording as a bounded themed quiz
[stderr] journey; it does not authorise an RPG campaign. Product decisions still marked
[stderr] approval-gated remain outside a complete first release.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Personas, jobs, and first-release promise
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Persona | Job / outcome | Journey supported |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | Casual adult player | In a few minutes, test football knowledge and get a fair, satisfying result. | J1 start-to-results; J2 replay. |
[stderr] | Returning player | Resume safely after interruption and see local improvement without redoing confirmed work. | J3 pause/recover/return. |
[stderr] | Accessibility-settings user | Read, operate, and understand every answer/result with their preferred presentation and input. | J0 configure; J1. |
[stderr] | Editorial contributor/reviewer | Produce original, factual, consistently adjudicated cards that are safe to release or correct. | J4 author-to-publish. |
[stderr] | Release/support operator | Stage a content update or explain recovery without losing confirmed player state. | J5 update/recovery. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] **Complete first-release journey (J1):** launch → optionally configure → enter
[stderr] the five-card `First Whistle` tutorial → answer/receive text-plus-audio/visual
[stderr] feedback → pause at a safe boundary if needed → finish results → create a
[stderr] confirmed local milestone/snapshot → exit and resume. It works with packaged
[stderr] content offline and no account, multiplayer, purchase, live event, or deferred
[stderr] dependency.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Core journeys and edge paths
[stderr] 
[stderr] | ID | Normal flow | Empty / invalid / denied / offline / conflict / recovery / deletion behaviour |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | J0 Settings and consent | Open settings before/during a round; changes apply immediately or next safe boundary and persist locally. | Invalid value restores last valid value with explanation. Optional diagnostic/notification denial leaves all play enabled. Reset settings confirms scope. |
[stderr] | J1 First Whistle | New local profile → tutorial → submit each answer → adjudication/explanation → results/snapshot. | Blank typed input cannot submit until explicitly confirm blank; malformed typed input resolves via normalisation then gives correction. No network is needed. Failure before a confirmed boundary offers retry/return home. |
[stderr] | J2 Standard round/replay | Choose available theme → deterministic 10-card selection → resolve → results → replay/choose/exit. | Empty eligible pool shows unavailable category and a different eligible choice; repeat shortage is disclosed. Invalid/stale content is ineligible. No ranked or remote conflict exists. |
[stderr] | J3 Pause, resume, recovery, deletion | Pause or interrupt → save confirmed snapshot → reopen → resume before next unresolved card. | Write failure preserves previous confirmed snapshot and offers retry/continue unsaved. Corrupt draft offers last confirmed snapshot/discard. Delete profile explicitly confirms and removes local history/snapshots/settings then returns to first launch. Remote conflict is not applicable: sync is excluded. |
[stderr] | J4 Editorial publish/correct | Propose → provenance → fact check → accessibility/copy edit → second review → versioned publish → validate → stage/release or rollback. | Missing provenance, ambiguous answer, failed validation, or reviewer rejection blocks publish. Rights/source uncertainty is escalated, not guessed. Offline authoring cannot publish. |
[stderr] | J5 Update/error support | Download/stage approved batch → apply between rounds → retain confirmed save → record minimum diagnostic only with consent. | Offline stays on cached compatible batch. Incompatible cache explains reset after save protection. Permission-denied diagnostics are skipped. Failed update rolls back/stays current; no mid-round replacement. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Domain relationship map and invariants
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```text
[stderr] Editorial content ─publishes→ Content version ─selects→ Round run
[stderr]      │ provenance/review                      │             │ attempts
[stderr]      └── blocks invalid cards                  │             ├─→ Adjudication ─→ Score/streak ─→ Results/milestone
[stderr]                                                │             │                         │
[stderr] Platform/cache ─provides→ input/rendering ─────┘             └─→ Save snapshot ─→ Recovery/delete
[stderr]      │                                                                        │
[stderr] Accessibility/settings ─applies to all player-facing nodes ──────────────────┘
[stderr] Release/diagnostics ─stages/observes versions and errors; never changes a live round
[stderr] Decision-gated identity/sync/safety/commerce have no first-release runtime edge.
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] Cross-domain invariants: a resolved attempt references immutable card/version
[stderr] and rule version; only published/reviewed cards may enter a round; score is a
[stderr] deterministic projection of attempts; confirmed snapshots are append/replace
[stderr] only after validation; content updates occur between rounds; local deletion
[stderr] removes all local profile-linked records; accessibility settings affect every
[stderr] path; diagnostics contain no answer text, typed answer, or unnecessary identity
[stderr] data. Lifecycle boundaries are content publish/rollback, round start/resolution/
[stderr] complete/abandon, snapshot confirmation/recovery/deletion, and cache stage/apply.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Domain chapters
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### A. Quiz shell, workflows, and player progress
[stderr] 
[stderr] **Entities/lifecycle:** `LocalProfile` (new → active → deletion-pending →
[stderr] deleted), `RoundRun` (created → active ↔ paused → completed | abandoned |
[stderr] recoverable), `QuestionAttempt` (presented → draft → submitted → resolved),
[stderr] and `ResultSummary` (computed → viewed → archived). **Rules:** one unresolved
[stderr] card at a time; a submission is immutable after resolution; results are
[stderr] idempotent; replay creates a new run. **Inputs/dependencies:** content version,
[stderr] selection seed, settings, persistence, input/rendering. **Outcome:** an
[stderr] understandable quick session. **Edge cases:** back during draft asks whether to
[stderr] discard; unavailable theme has an explanatory empty state; interruption creates
[stderr] recoverable state only at safe boundaries. **Boundary:** tutorial plus one
[stderr] standard template; no campaign, ranks, or social comparison.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### B. Question content, adjudication, and editorial production
[stderr] 
[stderr] **Entities/lifecycle:** cards/batches and review/provenance records are draft →
[stderr] review → published → superseded/withdrawn; a withdrawn card never enters a new
[stderr] round. **Rules:** schema, normalisation, quotas, provenance, two-editor review,
[stderr] and anti-repeat policy are GAME-001–004. **Authoring:** bounded `QB-A-01…48`
[stderr] and `TUT-01…05` cards with source/review fields; validators reject holes and
[stderr] distribution violations. **Dependencies:** editorial workflow, release/version,
[stderr] local repeat ledger. **Outcome:** fair topic breadth. **Edge cases:** disputed
[stderr] fact/rights uncertainty blocks release; answer alias collision requires rewrite;
[stderr] old run retains its referenced content version for explanation. **Boundary:**
[stderr] no scraping, AI-generated unreviewed facts, live feed, or unbounded catalogue.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### C. Round rules, score, streaks, and feedback
[stderr] 
[stderr] **Entities/lifecycle:** definitions are versioned; run/attempt/score events
[stderr] are created → resolved → summarised; streak resets per GAME-007. **Rules:**
[stderr] five fixed tutorial cards, ten standard cards, 100 base points and capped streak
[stderr] bonus; timer disabled by default. **Authoring inputs:** template, category,
[stderr] seed, feedback strings/cues. **Dependencies:** eligible cards, adjudication,
[stderr] save and accessibility. **Outcome:** transparent momentum, not punishment.
[stderr] **Edge cases:** blank/malformed/timeout/abandon reset streak; no eligible card
[stderr] creates empty state; versioned calculation prevents changed rules rewriting old
[stderr] results. **Boundary:** no paid boosts, daily competition, leaderboard, event,
[stderr] or difficulty multiplier.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### D. Persistence, offline cache, recovery, and privacy
[stderr] 
[stderr] **Entities/lifecycle:** snapshots draft → validated/confirmed → superseded →
[stderr] deleted; cache staged → active → obsolete/reset; `RecoveryRecord` is open →
[stderr] resolved. **Rules:** save only confirmed state at listed safe boundaries;
[stderr] preserve prior confirmed state on failure; deletion is confirmed and complete.
[stderr] **Inputs/dependencies:** platform storage, content version, optional diagnostic
[stderr] consent. **Outcome:** trustworthy return play. **Edge cases:** quota/write
[stderr] failure, process death, corrupt draft, cache mismatch, offline start, optional
[stderr] permission denial, and local deletion are J3/J5. **Boundary:** local-only
[stderr] profile/saves; remote identity/sync/conflict/retention is approval-gated.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### E. Presentation, input, accessibility, localisation, and original media
[stderr] 
[stderr] **Entities/lifecycle:** `Settings` is valid → applied → persisted/reset;
[stderr] `InputAction` is mapped → invoked; media cue is available/muted/unavailable.
[stderr] **Rules:** all critical actions have touch/pointer/keyboard/gamepad equivalent;
[stderr] semantic focus/labels and non-colour outcomes are mandatory; visual settings,
[stderr] text scaling, captions/text cues and reduced motion apply globally. **Authoring
[stderr] inputs:** original category visual tokens, localisable string keys, captions,
[stderr] cue metadata. **Dependencies:** shell, rendering/input adapters, settings.
[stderr] **Outcome:** equitable readable play. **Edge cases:** unsupported gamepad falls
[stderr] back visibly; missing audio leaves full text feedback; untranslated content is
[stderr] not offered as a language. **Boundary:** original broadcast-inspired system
[stderr] only; languages and exact audio asset count await approval.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### F. Delivery, targets, quality, and operations
[stderr] 
[stderr] **Entities/lifecycle:** `ContentVersion` draft → validated → staged → active →
[stderr] rolled-back; `DiagnosticEvent` queued → consented/withheld → sent/discarded.
[stderr] **Rules:** version switch only between rounds; cache refresh protects confirmed
[stderr] save; errors offer retry/home; diagnostics minimise data. **Authoring inputs:**
[stderr] release manifest, compatibility declaration, test evidence, privacy/store copy.
[stderr] **Dependencies:** platform packaging/PWA cache, content, recovery. **Outcome:**
[stderr] safe delivery on feasible networks. **Edge cases:** failed/partial update,
[stderr] offline cache, compatibility failure, error-report denial, and rollback are J5.
[stderr] **Boundary:** provider/CI/OS/browser matrix/performance and store policies await
[stderr] approval; no live event operation.
