[stderr] +# 03 — Technical, data, trust, and quality contract
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Inputs:** [`INITIAL.md`](../INITIAL.md), [domain discovery](00-domain-discovery.md),
[stderr] +[game identity](01-game-identity.md), [creative direction](01-creative-direction.md),
[stderr] +[feature model](02-feature-model.md), and [game design bible](02-game-design-bible.md).
[stderr] +
[stderr] +This contract implements the bounded first-release football-trivia game. It
[stderr] +does not turn the brief's approval-gated account, multiplayer, live-service,
[stderr] +commerce, or remote-sync requests into production scope. It specifies a
[stderr] +vendor-neutral architecture so those systems can be added only after their
[stderr] +identity, cost, safety, retention, and outage decisions are approved.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Production architecture and boundaries
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The release is an offline-capable 2D client game with one shared deterministic
[stderr] +domain core, immutable validated content packages, platform adapters, and local
[stderr] +durable storage. The initial web/PWA and Android/iOS outputs package the same
[stderr] +core and content; a platform adapter may render, persist, cache, map inputs,
[stderr] +report a fault locally, or obtain an approved release, but cannot adjudicate an
[stderr] +answer or alter a score. The core has no renderer, platform API, clock, network,
[stderr] +or third-party-service dependency.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Component / owned boundary | Product or quality requirement traced | Contract |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| Quiz application shell | GAME-005/008/009; J0–J3 | Owns routes, focus, pause/visibility prompts, ephemeral UI and accessible rendering. Sends intents to the core and never mutates a run directly. |
[stderr] +| Input and accessibility adapters | GAME-009/012; responsive web and phones | Map touch, pointer, keyboard, and gamepad to semantic actions (`navigate`, `select`, `submit`, `back`, `pause`). Apply text/contrast/reduced-motion/caption settings; unsupported hardware has a visible equivalent. |
[stderr] +| Deterministic quiz core | GAME-001, 003, 005–008 | Owns selection, normalisation/adjudication, score/streak, milestones, legal lifecycle transitions, and versioned rule calculations. Explicit seed and rule version make selection/results reproducible. |
[stderr] +| Content registry and validator | GAME-001–004; curated original bank | Resolves immutable published packages by stable ID and refuses invalid or withdrawn content before it can enter a new round. Runtime reads only validated data. |
[stderr] +| Save/recovery repository | GAME-008/010; J3 | Owns revisioned snapshots, checksum/validation, atomic promotion, rollback, migration, quarantine, export only if later approved, and confirmed deletion. |
[stderr] +| Release/cache manager | GAME-011/012; PWA/mobile offline delivery | Stages signed/hashed approved package and assets; activates only between rounds and never during a save commit. It retains a known-good compatible package on update failure. |
[stderr] +| Error boundary and diagnostics | crash recovery and privacy | Owns plain-language retry, return-home, and recovery choices. P0 diagnostics are local and consent-gated; no telemetry transport is assumed. |
[stderr] +| Editorial build tooling | J4/J5; factual/release integrity | Imports author-controlled source files, runs schema/relationship/provenance checks, and emits a content manifest. It has no runtime authoring or publishing endpoint. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +```text
[stderr] +authored content ─> build validator ─> immutable ContentPackage ─┐
[stderr] +                                                               ├─> deterministic quiz core <─ semantic input actions
[stderr] +platform renderer/accessibility <─ state + events ─────────────┘             │
[stderr] +             │                                                               ├─> save/recovery repository
[stderr] +             └─> release/cache manager (safe boundary only) ─────────────────┴─> local error/diagnostic record
[stderr] +```
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Only the core creates durable game facts. The shell owns transient selection,
[stderr] +focus, animation and open-panel state. The repository owns serialized records,
[stderr] +not gameplay. Content/cache, diagnostics, and UI must not be prerequisites for
[stderr] +a legal answer, score, or completed tutorial.
[stderr] +
