[stderr] +## Commands, validation, idempotency, and concurrency
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The core accepts typed intents: `CreateProfile`, `StartTutorial`, `StartRound`,
[stderr] +`SelectAnswer`, `EnterTypedAnswer`, `ConfirmBlank`, `SubmitAnswer`, `Pause`,
[stderr] +`Resume`, `CompleteRound`, `CommitSnapshot`, `RecoverSnapshot`, `DeleteProfile`,
[stderr] +and `ApplySettings`. Each state-changing intent carries `expectedRevision` and
[stderr] +a unique `interactionId`, and returns a typed rejection or ordered state/events
[stderr] +with a new revision.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Before mutation validate command shape/size, active lifecycle state,
[stderr] +  expected revision, content/rule compatibility, card eligibility, selected
[stderr] +  option or typed-answer normalisation, and required safe-boundary condition.
[stderr] +  Treat UI events, deep links, cached content and persisted bytes as untrusted.
[stderr] +- Typed answers use the GAME-003 deterministic Unicode/case/punctuation/
[stderr] +  whitespace/diacritic normalisation and configured aliases only—never fuzzy
[stderr] +  matching. Blank needs explicit confirmation; a resolved submission is
[stderr] +  immutable and shows canonical answer/explanation.
[stderr] +- `interactionId`, completed-run ID, milestone key and snapshot revision form
[stderr] +  idempotency keys. Retried submission/complete/snapshot returns its recorded
[stderr] +  result; it never adds score, streak, milestone, or history twice. A replay is
[stderr] +  a new run with a new selection seed.
[stderr] +- Process one intent per local profile/run. Disable/debounce submit while it is
[stderr] +  pending and reject an old revision after asynchronous persistence completes.
[stderr] +  A second browser tab or resumed process acquires a local lease or becomes
[stderr] +  read-only; a stale writer cannot replace the latest confirmed revision.
[stderr] +- Selection uses an explicit deterministic seed with content/rule version and
[stderr] +  local repeat ledger recorded in the snapshot. The last two completed rounds
[stderr] +  are excluded where possible; a shortage is a disclosed deterministic result,
[stderr] +  not a hidden reroll.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Persistence, migrations, and failure semantics
[stderr] +
[stderr] +At tutorial completion, every resolved-question boundary, explicit pause, and
[stderr] +completed result, save by: serialize a candidate → validate schema/checksum/
[stderr] +invariants → write immutable revision → read back/validate → atomically promote
[stderr] +current pointer → retain prior known-good revision. Storage must provide an
[stderr] +atomic final pointer or emulate one with revision records. It must never clear
[stderr] +the previous confirmed snapshot before promotion succeeds.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Condition | Required player-safe behaviour |
[stderr] +| --- | --- |
[stderr] +| Quota, permission denial, unavailable storage | Keep round playable, retain previous confirmed snapshot, state that saving failed, and offer retry/continue without saving. |
[stderr] +| Process death/interrupted write | Ignore incomplete candidate; load prior confirmed revision and offer the normal resume state. |
[stderr] +| Corrupt/checksum-invalid draft or snapshot | Quarantine bytes/metadata without overwrite; offer last known-good snapshot, discard draft, or new local profile. |
[stderr] +| Unsupported schema or migration failure | Preserve original candidate, fail closed into quarantine, and offer explicit recovery/new-game path. |
[stderr] +| Invalid/partial content/cache update | Keep compatible active package and save; block affected new-round route with retry/home explanation. Never activate it mid-round. |
[stderr] +| First offline visit/no cached package | Explain that initial approved download is needed; never misrepresent an uncached game as offline-ready. |
[stderr] +| Fault/crash loop | Error boundary offers retry, return home, and recovery; optional local diagnostics do not block either action. |
[stderr] +| Explicit deletion | Confirm scope, then remove profile/settings/history/snapshots/recovery records/local diagnostics and return to first launch. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Migrations are pure, ordered `fromSchema → toSchema` transformations with
[stderr] +fixtures for each supported predecessor. They run into a new candidate,
[stderr] +validate before promotion, and are idempotent or record source version so a
[stderr] +retry cannot apply one twice. A migration cannot reinterpret old answer facts,
[stderr] +grant new score/milestones, or change a completed run's content/rule reference.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Trust, privacy, security, and authorization
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- P0 has no server-owned resource and no player account: there is therefore no
[stderr] +  remote authorization role. A device/browser-profile owner can alter local
[stderr] +  data; local persistence is integrity/recovery protection, not anti-cheat.
[stderr] +  Editorial publication is an offline repository/release responsibility, not a
[stderr] +  client role. Any future server requires authenticated least-privilege roles,
[stderr] +  authorization on every request, rate limits, audit records, support owner,
[stderr] +  deletion/retention and outage/conflict policy before implementation.
[stderr] +- Persist only necessary local profile, game state, preferences, compatible
[stderr] +  content/cache and bounded recovery data. Do not collect names, contact data,
[stderr] +  precise location, ad IDs, payment data, account IDs, raw typed answers, or
[stderr] +  gameplay analytics. A diagnostic excludes question text, answer text, save
[stderr] +  payload and unique identity; consent describes fields, purpose, retention,
[stderr] +  deletion, and any approved transport.
[stderr] +- Validate and size-bound package, save, import, URL, platform event and
[stderr] +  service-worker message before parsing. Render authored text as text, never
[stderr] +  executable/unsafe HTML. Pin/review dependencies, scan generated release for
[stderr] +  secrets, use HTTPS and restrictive CSP/no third-party scripts for web builds,
[stderr] +  hash assets/manifests, and never embed credentials.
[stderr] +- All writing, art, visual asset and audio cue records carry provenance. The
[stderr] +  pipeline rejects copied reference expression and preserves source hash or
[stderr] +  original-work record. Functional references inform breadth/session goals only.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Target-platform matrix
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Exact minimum OS/browser, orientation, budgets, store metadata and distribution
[stderr] +providers remain release-approval gates. The following is the required target
[stderr] +contract, not a claim that each platform capability is universally available.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Contract | Responsive public web | PWA | Android phone | iPhone (iOS) |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| Shared code/data boundary | Shared core, schemas, package, actions, save semantics; web renderer/layout adapter only. | Same shared core/data; install/service-worker/cache adapter only. | Same shared core/data; native/web-runtime packaging, touch/accessibility/storage adapter only. | Same shared core/data; iOS packaging, touch/accessibility/storage adapter only. |
[stderr] +| Inputs/device capabilities | Keyboard, mouse, touch, gamepad when exposed; resize/visibility; feature-detect all. | Same; install/notification/storage prompts optional and non-blocking. | Touch first; orientation choice TBD; respect system text, contrast, motion, audio and focus affordances. | Touch first; orientation choice TBD; respect system text, contrast, motion, audio and focus affordances. |
[stderr] +| Offline and recovery | Offline only after assets/package cached; first uncached visit explains network need. Local save is independent of cache. | Installable offline route after successful cache; known-good cache survives refresh failure; safe update notice. | Packaged/cache-approved content and independent local save; offline core works after first installation; update only safe boundary. | Same as Android, subject to platform storage/cache behaviour; retain confirmed save across package/content update. |
[stderr] +| Build and test | Hashed static bundle/manifest; core/content/save unit tests; browser layout, keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad, slow-network and error checks. | Adds manifest/service worker; test install, offline reload, cache rollback, update-safe-boundary, cache/storage pressure. | Signed store-compatible build after approval; test physical/emulated representative touch, interrupt/resume, storage pressure, accessibility, battery/thermal/size budget. | Signed store-compatible build after approval; test representative devices, interrupt/resume, storage pressure, accessibility, battery/thermal/size budget. |
[stderr] +| Accessibility/performance | Semantic labels, focus, text scaling, contrast, captions/non-colour cues; measure approved load/frame/memory/bundle budgets across phone/tablet/desktop. | Same plus offline/update/install state is fully operable; measure cold/warm/offline startup and cache size. | Touch target, screen reader, text scaling, reduced motion/captions; measure startup/frame/memory/download/battery/thermal against approved thresholds. | Equivalent outcome using platform assistive tech; measure same approved mobile budgets and interrupted-state recovery. |
[stderr] +| Release channel/policy | Approved immutable static host; selected staged rollout/rollback; publish browser support, privacy and recovery notes. | Browser-mediated install/update; safe prompt, manifest/icon/display requirements, rollback retains runnable cache. | Approved Android distribution/store channel; complete privacy/data-safety, signing, age/content, accessibility and release-note requirements before submission. | Approved App Store/TestFlight channel; complete privacy nutrition label, signing, age/content, accessibility and review requirements before submission. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The shared game is capability-tested on current and previous agreed browser/OS
[stderr] +releases and representative phone, tablet and desktop classes. If an agreed
[stderr] +target lacks a capability, the app provides an understandable fallback or is
[stderr] +excluded by the approved support matrix—never silently weakens a core rule.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Observability, quality evidence, and release verification
[stderr] +
[stderr] +P0 observability is local and supportable: structured development/build logs,
[stderr] +visible package/save/cache version status, and optional minimal local fault
[stderr] +record. Every fault must have player-facing recovery and evidence that save or
[stderr] +cache protection held. External crash, analytics, account, commerce, live-op,
[stderr] +multiplayer/moderation, notification, and sync providers remain optional and
[stderr] +unintegrated until credentials, cost, data use, reliability and failure
[stderr] +behaviour receive approval.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Evidence layer | Required evidence before release |
[stderr] +| --- | --- |
[stderr] +| Rules/content | Unit/property fixtures for formats/normalisation, illegal lifecycle commands, scoring cap/reset, deterministic seeds/repeat exclusion, immutable results/idempotency, card schema/provenance/review/distribution/reference/localisation/asset/cue validation. |
[stderr] +| Save/recovery | Encode/decode/checksum, atomic-promotion sequence, concurrent/stale revision, write/quota failure, crash restart, corrupt draft, every migration predecessor, content compatibility, delete-profile and no-double-completion fixtures. |
[stderr] +| Integration | Shell-to-core action mapping; tutorial offline completion; focus/pause/resume; missing audio/input fallback; settings persistence failure; package update between rounds; cache/save independence; error retry/home paths. |
[stderr] +| Targets/accessibility | Matrix checks for responsive viewport, keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad paths, PWA install/offline/update, Android/iOS touch/interruption/storage, semantic/focus/manual assistive-technology checks, text/contrast/reduced-motion/captions. |
[stderr] +| Performance/security | Measured approved initial/warm/offline load, frame, memory, cache/download, slow-network, battery and thermal budgets; dependency/license/provenance/secrets review; CSP/HTTPS/manifest hash checks; parser bounds/fuzz tests. |
[stderr] +| Release gate | Clean content validation; compatibility declaration; migration/recovery suite; target build/install evidence; PWA rollback/offline check; accessibility/performance results; store/privacy copy; known-good content and app rollback rehearsal. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Release is blocked if a package can select unpublished/ambiguous content, a
[stderr] +save can replace the last valid snapshot, an update can switch mid-round or
[stderr] +mid-write, core play lacks an accessible fallback, or a required approved
[stderr] +matrix/budget/policy evidence item is absent.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Approval-gated decisions
[stderr] +
[stderr] +This contract deliberately does not select engine/framework, rendering library,
[stderr] +storage implementation, static host/CDN, CI, signing/distribution tooling,
[stderr] +diagnostic vendor/transport, content editor, exact support matrix/orientation,
[stderr] +performance/download/battery/thermal budgets, languages, audio count, or
[stderr] +regional/age/store policy. Account/identity, remote sync and conflict handling,
[stderr] +multiplayer safety, live operations, analytics, IAP/entitlements, seasonal
[stderr] +content and player-created/shared content require separate product, security,
[stderr] +privacy, cost, operational ownership and failure-semantics approval. Until
[stderr] +then they cannot be implicit dependencies of the playable offline release.
[stderr] 
